{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17147-books-with-god-machine-hints","id":17147,"title":"Books with God-Machine hints","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-24T09:12:06-08:00","id":17147,"title":"Books with God-Machine hints","content":"Obviously I'm just tempting myself to spend tons of money I don't have, but it's obvious now that many books had G-M hints in them. I know there were hints in the original WoD book and Second Sight. That vampire covenant that could hear the God-Machine was a hint too, I suppose. What other books give some hints or insight to the G-M. Where else across the WoD are clues embedded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:50:51-08:00","id":17244,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't view them as &quot;hints&quot; or &quot;clues&quot; so much as writers taking off from a popular section of the corebook, but here are some further pre-GMC mentions of the mythos.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine Chronicle Anthology reprints two stories from <b>Mysterious Places</b> and <b>Urban Legends</b> that are clear touches of the God-Machine; Eggs, the story from Urban Legends, is the first appearance of the Deva Corporation. (Residents, the story from Mysterious Places, is fantastic.) The Promethean supplement <b>Saturnine Night</b> has an adventure that culminates in the discovery of a vast God-Machine facility beneath Detroit. The Mage supplement <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> speculates on one possible explanation for the God-Machine's origin and motives, at least one rumored among mages. Again with Mage, the <b>Tome of the Watchtowers</b> has an anecdote about the Oracle of the Aether ascending into a clockwork god-machine undergirding reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:55:23-08:00","id":17354,"title":"","content":"The Fiction Anthology reproduces a number of stories from various books; I have to second Residents as being one of the best (with The Road Gospel as my other favorite, but only because I loved Midnight Roads). Saturnine Night discusses The Principle and gives explanations as to what it is; one of the answers literlly says &quot;a God-Machine&quot; and describes the thing we know and love today. There's the aforementioned Vampire covenant dedicated to the G-M (what book was that in?), and I'm convinced I'm missing one other thing somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T16:15:11-08:00","id":17364,"title":"","content":"Slashers has a fella who gains hints of the Godmachine the utterances of those he removes the arms and legs of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17147-books-with-god-machine-hints?p=17354#post17354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fiction Anthology reproduces a number of stories from various books; I have to second Residents as being one of the best (with The Road Gospel as my other favorite, but only because I loved Midnight Roads). Saturnine Night discusses The Principle and gives explanations as to what it is; one of the answers literlly says &quot;a God-Machine&quot; and describes the thing we know and love today. There's the aforementioned Vampire covenant dedicated to the G-M (what book was that in?), and I'm convinced I'm missing one other thing somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Covenant is in Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}